# ── openEHR Task Planning (PROC) — the higher-fidelity by-reference bridge ────

logic:Plan skos:relatedMatch <https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/PROC/latest/task_planning.html#WORK_PLAN> {|
    a logic:GroundingCorrespondence ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-logic-openehr-task-planning.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7 ;
    gmeow:objectLabel "openEHR Task Planning WORK_PLAN" ;
    gmeow:comment "An openEHR WORK_PLAN is the top-level plan a care team executes (by reference — openEHR PROC publishes no canonical RDF). A top-level logic:Plan lowers onto it with HIGHER fidelity than onto any acyclic engine: TP-VML/DLM carries loops and guarded branching on real conditions, so a logic:Iteration or a logic:Choice in the program body projects faithfully rather than unrolling. The residue is confined to concurrency and compensation." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "logic:ConcurrentComposition: under-approximated where TP-VML has no explicit concurrency-serializability guarantee (logic:ConcurrentHistory / logic:serializabilityCriterion are derived natively, not carried)" ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "per-outcome logic:compensation: omitted where TP-VML has no compensation primitive on a task outcome" ;
    logic:sourceEndpoint logic:Plan ;
    logic:targetEndpoint <https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/PROC/latest/task_planning.html#WORK_PLAN> ;
    logic:morphismClass logic:BridgeView ;
    logic:morphismKind logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:ValidationOnly
|} .

logic:Plan skos:relatedMatch <https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/PROC/latest/task_planning.html#TASK_PLAN> {|
    a logic:GroundingCorrespondence ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-logic-openehr-task-planning.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.65 ;
    gmeow:objectLabel "openEHR Task Planning TASK_PLAN / SUB_PLAN" ;
    gmeow:comment "An openEHR TASK_PLAN (and its SUB_PLAN nesting) is a constituent plan hanging under a work plan (by reference). The logic: counterpart is a sub-plan: a logic:Plan reached as an operand of its parent's program tree through logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand / logic:iterationBody from the parent's logic:planBody root. The nesting round-trips; the confidence is below the WORK_PLAN row because the sub-plan boundary is a positional fact in openEHR and a structural one in logic:." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "the sub-plan boundary: openEHR marks it with a distinct TASK_PLAN/SUB_PLAN container, while logic: reads it off the parent's program-tree operand structure, so the container identity is not preserved" ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "per-outcome logic:compensation: omitted where TP-VML has no compensation primitive on a task outcome" ;
    logic:sourceEndpoint logic:Plan ;
    logic:targetEndpoint <https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/PROC/latest/task_planning.html#TASK_PLAN> ;
    logic:morphismClass logic:BridgeView ;
    logic:morphismKind logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:ValidationOnly
|} .

logic:ActionSchema skos:relatedMatch <https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/PROC/latest/task_planning.html#TASK> {|
    a logic:GroundingCorrespondence ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-logic-openehr-task-planning.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7 ;
    gmeow:objectLabel "openEHR Task Planning TASK / TASK_ACTION" ;
    gmeow:comment "An openEHR TASK / TASK_ACTION is the executable unit of a task plan (by reference). A logic:ActionSchema lowers onto it, and three DLM constructs are SUBSUMED natively rather than merely bridged: a DLM-gated task is a guarded logic:Choice (preserved, not unrolled); a manual-notification task is a logic:NotificationWaitSchema; and a currency-guarded task input is a logic:FreshnessGuard on BOTH its axes — `currency` (maximum datum age) onto logic:freshnessHorizon and `time_window` (an explicit valid-time interval) onto logic:freshnessWindow / logic:freshnessWindowStart / logic:freshnessWindowEnd." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "TP-VML task scheduling annotations (planned time, wait windows) are not carried by a bare logic:ActionSchema; scheduling is a solver-layer concern (Principle 12)" ;
    logic:sourceEndpoint logic:ActionSchema ;
    logic:targetEndpoint <https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/PROC/latest/task_planning.html#TASK> ;
    logic:morphismClass logic:BridgeView ;
    logic:morphismKind logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:ValidationOnly
|} .
